jitFlagPlusT -- F-131 (SEQ 364) on the jit road; flagPlusT is the kant road, interpreted.
  JFP-0  control: an unflagged count, ++ jitted, 5 -> 6
  JFP-F  the flag really is set (read after the ++)
  JFP-1  a flagged count, ++ jitted, reads 6. Born red on trunk: copy 1 of opPlusPlus's fLAG read sits above the
         jitting gate, so at EMIT time it returned 0 and no increment was emitted.
The flag is set in jfSet, interpreted, because `:. flaG` inside a jitted action refuses (`:. tempField` -- Clod's
jitSetFlagTemp fixit). For the same reason there is no iterator row here: iterate clears fLAG and `:.` cannot set it
under jit, so a jitted iterator never carries the flag. Copy 2 guards the interpreted iterator only (flagPlusT FP-3).
testing() routes a coded action to jitRunAction (bear-trap #25); flagPlusT is the interpreted oracle, its own process.
